# Soma's plan, in John Carmack's .plan format: one item per line, under the
# day it was written. An unmarked line is open; "* " marks one done that day,
# "+ " one done later, "- " one dropped. The order is the priority. An item is
# a pointer: its details are in the files it names. Pantheon's docs/PLAN.md
# explains how its market drafts tasks from this file.

2026-11-09
+ S-2: refuse a `Rocq Library` package or version that isn't one safe path component, so "../" can't escape Soma's cache and a leading "-" can't reach opam (SECURITY-REVIEW.md S-2; plugins/soma_rocq/soma_rocq.ml ensure; a test in test-suite)
+ S-3: refuse a soma.lock whose commit isn't 40 hexadecimal digits, before anything is removed or fetched (SECURITY-REVIEW.md S-3; vernac/somaDeps.ml read_lock)
+ S-1: don't trust a .soma-cache this build didn't write: refuse git-tracked cache files, key the shared cache by the Soma build too, publish only what this build wrote (SECURITY-REVIEW.md S-1; vernac/somaImport.ml ensure, topbin/soma.ml)
S-5: confine `Extraction "FILE"` and `Redirect` output to the project being built, refusing absolute paths and ../ (SECURITY-REVIEW.md S-5; plugins/extraction/extract_env.ml, vernac/synterp.ml)
Declare ML Module: refuse it however it's spaced or commented, deciding on the parsed command, not a text search (SECURITY-REVIEW.md "Known limits"; plugins/soma_rocq/soma_rocq.ml)
